-5893352-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5893352</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1132598A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MASHIKI ZENICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA MOTOR CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASHIKI, ZENICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA JIDOSHA KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MASHIKI ZENICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASHIKI, ZENICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUNO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A device and method for control of an engine having a fuel injection valve (40) directly injecting fuel into a combustion chamber (16), wherein a fuel feed device includes a feed pump (46) and a booster pump (47), the booster pump (47) further pressurizes the fuel fed from the feed pump (46) at a specified pressure so as to feed it to the fuel injection valve (40), the driving of the booster pump (47) is stopped so that the fuel injection valve (40) can inject fuel at the pressure of fuel fed from the feed pump (46) when a trouble occurs on the booster pump (47), and the amount of air for driving the fuel injection valve (40) or sucked into the combustion chamber (16) is limited so that only air/fuel mixture not inducing misfire is formed in the combustion chamber (16) when the driving of the booster pump (47) is stopped, whereby such an air/fuel mixture that may induce misfire is not formed in the combustion chamber (16), ignition to the air/fuel mixture in the fuel chamber (16) is assured, and the unburned air/fuel mixture is not exhausted from the combustion chamber (16).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On décrit un dispositif et un procédé de commande destiné à un moteur comportant une soupape (40) d'injection de carburant qui injecte directement le carburant dans une chambre (16) de combustion. Dans ce dispositif,n dispositif d'alimentation en carburant comprend une pompe (46) d'alimentation et une pompe (47) de suralimentation, cette dernière (47) mettant sous pression le carburant envoyé par la pompe (46) d'alimentation à une pression spécifiée de manière à l'envoyer à la soupape (40) d'injection de carburant ; la commande de la pompe (47) de suralimentation est arrêtée pour que la soupape (40) d'injection de carburant puisse injecter le carburant à la pression du carburant envoyé par la pompe (46) d'alimentation lorsque la pompe (47) de suralimentation connaît un problème, et la quantité d'air qui est destinée à commander la soupape (40) d'injection de carburant ou qui est aspirée dans la chambre (16) de combustion est limitée pour que seul le mélange air/carburant n'induisant pas des ratés soit formé dans la chambre (16) de combustion lorsque la commande de la pompe (47) de suralimentation est arrêtée, ceci permettant de ne pas former dans la chambre (16) de combustion un mélange air/carburant pouvant induire des ratés, d'assurer l'allumage du mélange air/carburant dans la chambre (16) de combustion et d'assurer que le mélange air/carburant non brûlé ne sorte pas de la chambre (16) de combustion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>